/* THE INK PALETTE.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Every colour in this app was written as a GLOW: a translucent fill of some
   hue with a pale tint of that same hue as the text. On the dark ground that is
   correct — the fill lifts and the pale ink sits brightly on it. On a white
   sheet both move the wrong way: the fill goes darker than the ground and the
   ink goes lighter than its own fill, so a crew chip lands at 1.17:1.

   The fix is not to pick new colours. It is to keep the hue and invert the
   value — same family, deep instead of pale — and that is a token's job, not a
   component's. Each name below holds its EXACT current value here, so the dark
   theme is byte-identical; the flip block redefines them for paper.

   Values below are derived, not hand-picked: hue preserved, saturation capped
   at 0.72 so nothing goes electric, lightness solved until it clears 5.6:1 on
   white (a pale wash of the same hue still leaves it above 4.5:1). Greys with
   no real hue are not colours at all and join the text ramp instead. */
