/* THE WORKBENCH FLIP. One block re-themes every paper container's subtree.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Custom properties inherit, so redeclaring the surface tokens here re-points
   every `rgba(var(--tint), α)`, every `var(--text)` and every `var(--muted)`
   inside a card — about two thousand declarations — without a single component
   rule knowing that it happened. This is the whole mechanism.

   `color-scheme: light` matters as much as the colours: it is what makes a
   <select>, a date picker and a scrollbar inside a sheet render light.

   The popovers, menus and modals below are in this list for one reason: they
   OPEN FROM A SHEET. Each of them painted a literal navy and then inherited the
   sheet's dark ink on top of it, so every one was black text on a black box at
   1.0:1. None of it shows in a screenshot — these surfaces only exist after a
   click, which is exactly how they all survived the first pass. A surface that
   opens from Workbench paper is paper. Sunlight and Parchment already define
   complete root palettes; including them here would flatten both into the same
   generic cool-grey card palette. */
