/* THREE COLUMNS ON A PHONE IS WHY THE WHOLE APP PANNED SIDEWAYS.
   This grid had no narrow rule at all, so a 390px phone got three tracks of
   ~89px holding cards whose contents do not go below ~155px. `minmax(0, 1fr)`
   lets the TRACK shrink but a grid item still lays out at its own min-content
   and overflows, and a mobile browser answers content wider than the viewport
   by widening the layout viewport: measured 534px of layout on a 390px device,
   497px on a 320px one. That is a whole app you can pan right on, on every page
   carrying this grid — which is most of them.

   Two columns before one, because these cards are a label and a figure and a
   pair of them still reads on a phone. The .compact, .condensed, .four-up and
   .calendar-heading-metrics variants all set their own templates in compound
   selectors, so they win on specificity and are untouched. */
