/* THE COLLAPSE THAT NEVER FIRED, MOVED TO WHERE IT CAN.
   `@media (max-width: 900px) { .form-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr } }` has
   been in this file for a long time at ~line 7970 — ABOVE the declaration it is
   meant to override. A media query adds no specificity, so at equal weight the
   later rule wins and the collapse has never fired for anybody. The booking
   page found this and repaired it inside .book-scope only, deliberately leaving
   the shared rule for "its own mobile pass". This is that pass.

   Measured at 320px before: the new-job intake form's fields were 535px inside
   a 320px viewport, which widened the layout viewport to 342 and let every page
   carrying a two-column form pan sideways.

   minmax(0, 1fr) and not 1fr, and min-width: 0 on the children: `1fr` is
   `minmax(auto, 1fr)` so the track cannot go under its content's min-content,
   and a bare <input> refuses to shrink below its default 20-character size.
   One column alone would not have been enough. */
@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .form-grid {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }

  .form-grid>* {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .form-grid input,
  .form-grid select,
  .form-grid textarea {
    max-width: 100%;
  }
}

