}

.ins-payhealth-note {
  margin-top: 0.5rem;
}

/* Top opportunities — the ranked "do this next" list.

   THE PRIORITY BADGES, AND EVERY CHIP THAT SHARES THEIR INK. Each of these
   pairs a tinted pill with a matching ink, and the tint is an rgba of the DARK
   theme's hue — so the pill lightens on paper while the ink stayed put. Measured
   in the light theme: "Do first" 2.12:1, "Worth doing" 1.96:1, and the eleven
   .ins-chip glyphs between 1.60 and 2.36. Colour is the whole signal on a badge
   that says one word, so this is not a legibility nicety.

   Every literal here is now the --ink-* token whose DARK value is that literal,
   which makes this a no-op on the canvas and a real change on the sheet. Four
   of them (blue-2, green-13, violet-5) had no token yet and are new; the rest
   already existed. On paper they measure 4.58–6.79:1 against their own pill. */
.ins-opps {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.ins-opp {
